        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 18:2",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Then I went down to the potter’s house, and, behold, he wrought a work on the wheels.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 18:3",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And the vessel that he made of clay was marred in the hand of the potter: so he made it again another vessel, as seemed good to the potter to make it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 147,
            "end": 150
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 18:4",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Then the word of the Lord came to me, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 18:5",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "O house of Israel, cannot I do with you as this potter? saith the Lord. Behold, as the clay is in the potter’s hand, so are ye in mine hand, O house of Israel.",
